<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Dec 14.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Dec 14.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to Dec 14 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week Dec 08-Dec 14</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97	 923,833 tns	 88,266 tns     9.55 pct</p>
<p>     95-96	 178,755 tns	  8,772 tns     4.91 pct</p>
<p>     94-95	 767,134 tns	 73,170 tns     9.54 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to Dec 14</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     2,359,374 tns	206,378 tns     8.75 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,735,364 tns	143,508 tns     8.27 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     2,128,724 tns	187,668 tns     8.82 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week 35 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 32 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 36 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9530</p>
</text>
